---
# The second backup target. Longhorn has supported more than one since v1.8.0, and a volume
# picks its target through its own spec.backupTargetName — RecurringJob has no target field,
# so daily-backup and weekly-backup keep scheduling exactly as before and each volume's
# backups simply land wherever it points.
#
# Named `r2` rather than replacing `default`: `default` stays B2's, so the routing lists in
# defaults/main.yml are the only thing that decides where a volume goes, and emptying
# k3s_longhorn_r2_volumes returns everything to B2 without touching this object.
#
# Armed independently of B2. k3s_longhorn_backup_armed is the incident lever for B2's
# transaction caps; R2 has its own allowance and its own failure modes, so one being blanked
# must not blank the other. Same enforcement semantics though — a disarmed run writes an
# empty backupTargetURL rather than leaving whatever is live.
apiVersion: longhorn.io/v1beta2
kind: BackupTarget
metadata:
  name: r2
  namespace: longhorn-system
spec:
  backupTargetURL: "{% if k3s_longhorn_r2_armed | bool %}s3://{{ r2_bucket }}@{{ k3s_longhorn_r2_region }}/{{ k3s_longhorn_r2_backup_prefix }}{% endif %}"
  credentialSecret: longhorn-r2
  # Seconds, rendered as the duration string the CR wants. See k3s_longhorn_r2_poll_interval.
  pollInterval: "{{ k3s_longhorn_r2_poll_interval }}s"
